Intercept vs Middleware
Example: When You Need an Interceptor

Log both request and response

Measure response time

Transform responses

Handle errors globally


Use middleware for request-level logic (e.g., IP logging, simple request data).
Use interceptors for complete control over request-response flow, timing, and logging.

Use Middleware when:
You need to run logic before the route handler only

You are dealing with raw HTTP stuff (like req, res)

You want to do:

Simple request logging

Basic authentication checks

CORS headers

Rate limiting

Parsing, IP logging, etc.

if (!req.headers['x-api-key']) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');

✅ Use Interceptors when:
You want to log both request & response

You want to measure response time

You want to transform responses (e.g. wrap all responses in { data: ... })

You want to catch and handle errors

You need access to controller method return values

You work inside NestJS-style lifecycle (RxJS, Observables, DI)

🧠 Think of interceptors as: “I want to watch or modify the entire request-response lifecycle.”
